        "Nickel Alloy 201":
          "A low-carbon variant (UNS N02201) specifically engineered for service at temperatures exceeding 600°F (315°C). The reduced carbon prevents embrittlement, ensuring the material remains ductile and structurally sound in high-heat environments.",
