    shortDescription:
      "Premium nickel fasteners manufacturer, supplier and exporter based in Mumbai, India, operating since 2013. Nickel fasteners are bolting components machined from commercially pure nickel bar supplied to ASTM B160 / ASME SB-160, with nickel at a minimum of 99.0%. Available in Nickel 200 (UNS N02200) for general corrosive service and Nickel 201 (UNS N02201) for elevated-temperature applications. Diameters range from M6 to M24 in metric sizes and from 1/4 in to 1-1/2 in in imperial sizes.",
    technicalOverview:
      "Nickel fasteners are bolting components machined from commercially pure nickel bar supplied to ASTM B160 / ASME SB-160, with nickel at a minimum of 99.0%. The high nickel content provides strong resistance to caustic soda, while Nickel 200 and Nickel 201 are also used in applications involving dry chlorine and hydrogen fluoride. Their commercially pure nickel chemistry can also be advantageous where material purity is important. Nickel 200 is suited to general corrosive service, while the lower carbon content of Nickel 201 makes it more suitable for prolonged exposure to elevated temperatures. Bolts, screws, studs and nuts are machined from certified nickel bar to ASTM B160 / ASME SB-160, which covers Nickel 200 (UNS N02200) and Nickel 201 (UNS N02201). There is no ASTM fastener specification covering commercially pure nickel, so dimensions, head form and thread form are supplied to the dimensional standard called out on the drawing, whether ASME, ISO, DIN, IS or JIS.",
