    shortDescription:
      "Premium Copper Nickel (Cupro-Nickel) wires in 90/10 (C70600) and 70/30 (C71500) grades, engineered for high-performance electrical, marine, and industrial applications. Offering a unique combination of electrical resistivity, thermal stability, and extraordinary resistance to seawater corrosion. Ideal for marine engineering, offshore platforms, desalination plants, and specialized electrical applications.",

    technicalOverview:
      "Copper Nickel (CuNi) wires, often referred to as Cupro-Nickel, are specialized alloy products engineered for high-performance electrical, marine, and industrial applications. By alloying copper with nickel—typically ranging from 10% to 30%—and adding controlled amounts of iron and manganese, these wires achieve a unique combination of electrical resistivity, thermal stability, and extraordinary resistance to seawater corrosion. The defining feature of Copper Nickel is its natural anti-fouling property, forming a thin, protective oxide film in marine environments that inhibits the attachment of biological organisms like barnacles and algae, maintaining the efficiency of submerged components over long service life. CuNi 90/10 is the most widely utilized grade for general marine engineering and low-resistance electrical applications, containing approximately 10% nickel and 1.5% iron. It offers exceptional resistance to stress corrosion cracking and pitting in clean seawater, is highly ductile and easy to cold-work, and offers moderate electrical resistance and high thermal conductivity. CuNi 70/30 contains approximately 30% nickel and is designed for more demanding service conditions involving higher fluid velocities and pressures, with superior tensile strength and hardness maintaining structural integrity at elevated temperatures and pressures.",

