        "Stainless Steel 316L":
          "The low-carbon version (UNS S31603 / 1.4404) specially formulated with reduced carbon to prevent intergranular corrosion during welding. The preferred choice for heavy-gauge components, complex fabrications, and high-hygiene sectors such as food processing and pharmaceutical medical devices.",
