    shortDescription:
      "Premium Hastelloy B3 (UNS N10675 / 2.4600) nickel-molybdenum alloy pipes engineered for exceptional resistance to hydrochloric acid and improved thermal stability. Manufactured to ASTM B622, B619 and ASME SB622, SB619 standards.",

    technicalOverview:
      "Hastelloy B3, identified by the technical designations UNS N10675 and 2.4600, is an advanced nickel-molybdenum alloy that serves as the next generation of the B-series family. While it retains the excellent resistance to hydrochloric acid found in its predecessor, B2, it features a significantly improved level of thermal stability. The alloy's precise chemistry includes a combination of nickel and molybdenum, supplemented by carbon, manganese, chromium, iron, silicon, tungsten, aluminum, cobalt, and titanium. A critical technical advantage of Hastelloy B3 pipes is their ability to resist grain-boundary precipitation in the heat-affected zone during welding. Furthermore, the high nickel content significantly reduces the risk of trans-granular stress corrosion cracking when exposed to chloride solutions. These pipes remain highly flexible even during transitory exposure to intermediate temperatures, preserving the high ductility necessary for successful heat treatment and complex fabrication.",

