    shortDescription:
      "Premium Hastelloy B2 (UNS N10665 / 2.4617) nickel-molybdenum alloy pipes engineered for superior resistance to reducing environments, particularly hydrochloric acid. Manufactured to ASTM B622, B619 and ASME SB622, SB619 standards.",

    technicalOverview:
      "Hastelloy B2, also identified by the designations UNS N10665 and 2.4617, is a solid-solution-strengthened nickel-molybdenum alloy. Unlike the C-series Hastelloy grades, B2 is specifically engineered for superior resistance to reducing environments. Its chemical composition is characterized by a high molybdenum content, which provides significant resistance to hydrochloric acid across all concentrations and a wide range of temperatures. The alloy is designed to resist the formation of grain-boundary carbide precipitates in the weld heat-affected zone, making it suitable for most chemical process applications in the as-welded condition. Furthermore, Hastelloy B2 pipes exhibit high tensile strength and can maintain their structural integrity at both cryogenic and extremely high temperatures. The addition of tungsten and specialized annealing processes further enhance these mechanical properties, making the pipes a reliable choice for high-pressure and high-temperature process plants.",

